the advantages of lambda expression,
1.it will reduce the byte code
2.lenght of the code also reduced

syntax: arguments->expression
the lambda expression will provide the imple of only functional interfaces..java 1.8


example 1:
case1:Application without lambda
interface Message{
void wish();
}
class Ratan implements Message
{
public void wish(){
sout("good morning");
}
}
class TestClient{
psvm{
Ratan r=new Ratan();
r.wish();
}
}

case2:

Application with lambda
interface Message
{
void wish();
}
psvm{
Message m1=()->sout("good morning");;
m1.wish();

Message m2=()->{
sout ("aaruu..");sout("annu");};
m2.wish();
}
}//in lambda when we take the multiple print statement take that statements in braces

example 2:
lambda with arguments:
interface Operations
{
void add(int num1,int num2);
}
class TestClient
{
psvm{
Operation op1=(int num1,int num2)->sout(num1+num2);
op1.add(10,20);

Operation op2=(num1,num2)->sout(num1 + num2);
op2.add(100,200);
}
}//in lambda while taking arguments the type declaration is optional


example 3:
lambda with return type
interface Operation
{
psvm{
Operation op1=(username)->{ return "good morning".....+username;};
String result1=op1.disp("ratan");

Operation op2=(username)->"good evening..."+ username;
String result2=op2.disp("anuu");
sout(result2);

}
}
in lambda exp only return value is present, then specifying the return stmt is optional.

